*---------------------- HEADER FIELD
* Hand-written for Prism's ROX tests (public domain). 5 keys + scratch, one background sound.

#PLAYER 1
#GENRE Test
#TITLE ROX BMS features
#SUBTITLE [FEATURES]
#ARTIST Prism
#BPM 120
#BPM01 180
#STOP01 48
#PLAYLEVEL 5
#DIFFICULTY 3
#LNTYPE 1
#LNOBJ ZZ

#WAV01 song.ogg
#WAV02 kick.wav
#WAV03 snare.wav

* #RANDOM always draws 1 in ROX: the first branch is read.
#RANDOM 2
#IF 1
#TITLE ROX BMS features (first branch)
#ENDIF
#IF 2
#TITLE never read
#ENDIF

*---------------------- MAIN DATA FIELD

* measure 0 (120 BPM): the background sound, a kick, a snare on key 1 and on the scratch
#00001:01
#00011:02000300
#00016:0003

* measure 1: BPM 180 from its start (channel 08 reads #BPM01), four notes
#00108:01
#00111:02020202

* measure 2 is half as long; one note in its middle
#00202:0.5
#00212:0003

* measure 3: a stop of one beat (#STOP01 48) at its start; a tap, and the head of a #LNOBJ long note
#00309:01
#00311:02
#00313:02

* measure 4: the #LNOBJ terminator (not a note), a mine on key 1, the head of a channel-5x long note
#00413:ZZ
#004D1:0A00
#00454:02

* measure 5: the end of the channel-5x long note, two taps
#00554:02
#00511:03
#00515:02
